>> title: Ox Tails
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, braise, southern, gravy, slow
>> counters: Meat and Three, One Pot
>> aka: oxtails, ox tail, braised oxtails, smothered oxtails, oxtail and gravy
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 45 min
>> slack: forgiving — oxtail is only ever undercooked, never over: stop early and you are handing someone a cut of tail to fight
>> pairs-with: cheese-grits, collard-greens, butter-beans, hoppin-john
>> washing-up: the Dutch oven, a cup to slake the cornstarch in
>> keeps: 4 days — the tails set the sauce to a jelly by themselves, and the meat is better on the second day

>> step: Braise until the meat slips off the bone without help. The gravy's stickiness comes out of the bone.
Braise these until the meat slips off the bone without help.

>> step: season, both sides
Season @beef oxtails{4%lb}(1.8 kg; cut in sections) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{2%tsp}.

>> step: brown 12 min, in batches
Brown @&(~1)seasoned oxtails{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #Dutch oven{} for ~brown{12%min}, in two batches.

>> step: braise covered 325°F 3 hr
Braise @&(~1)browned oxtails{} covered with @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @garlic{6%cloves}(smashed), @carrots{2}(cut in chunks), @beef stock{4%cup}(950 mL), @dry red wine{1%cup}(240 mL), @bay leaves{2}, @dried thyme{1%tsp} at 325°F (165°C) for ~braise{3%hr}.

>> step: skim, then slake the starch in
Skim @&(~1)braised oxtails{}, then stir in @cornstarch{1%Tbs}(8 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) and ~simmer{5%min}.

Spoon it over rice or cheese grits. Most of what is in the pot is gravy and the plate needs something under it.
